# Security Practices

## Critical Rules

- Never expose secrets, API keys, or credentials in code or source control
- Always use HTTPS in production; validate and sanitize user input; never trust external data

## XSS Prevention

- React escapes text by default; **avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`** unless necessary
- If you must render HTML: sanitize with **DOMPurify** — `DOMPurify.sanitize(html, { ALLOWED_TAGS, ALLOWED_ATTR })`; restrict to safe tags/attrs and `ALLOWED_URI_REGEXP: /^https?:\\/\\//i` for links
- **Links:** Validate `href` protocol (`http:`/`https:` only); use `rel="noopener noreferrer"` for `target="_blank"`

## Secure Storage

- **Tokens:** Prefer memory + HttpOnly cookies for refresh; avoid localStorage for tokens if possible
- **Sensitive data:** Do not store in localStorage/sessionStorage unless encrypted and necessary; clear on logout

## CSP (Content Security Policy)

- Set CSP headers (e.g. in server or Vite middleware): `default-src 'self'`; restrict `script-src`, `style-src`, `connect-src` to known origins; avoid `'unsafe-inline'` where possible

## CORS and API

- API should allow only needed origins; credentials only when required; frontend uses same-origin or configured API URL

## Best Practices

- Sanitize all user-derived HTML; validate URLs; secure storage for tokens; CSP; no secrets in client bundle

## Anti-Patterns

- `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with unsanitized input; `javascript:` or unvalidated hrefs; secrets in code or localStorage; missing CSP

**See also:** `input-sanitization.mdc`, `validation.mdc`
